; The far-call module of a program with no `farcall` entry in its environment file: every
; region is in fixed memory, so a `with` block has nothing to map (provisional, 2026-11-14;
; lathe/docs/configurations.md, "The far-call run-time modules").
;
; The compiler calls `rt_with.map` at the start of each `with REGION do ... end` and
; `rt_with.unmap` where the block is left. With a `farcall MODULE` entry the linker reads those
; names as MODULE's (rt_bank.map, rt_bank.unmap); with none, build.py links this module, as it
; links rt_frame, and they are these: a lone RTS each.
;
;     LDA #bank(REGION)        ; 0: the region is fixed
;     JSR rt_with.map          ; gives the old bank in A: here, A as it was
;     STA temporary
;     ...
;     LDY temporary
;     JSR rt_with.unmap        ; keeps A, X, Y and the flags
module rt_with

; Map the bank `value` into the window; give the bank that was there.
pub asm func map(value: byte in a): byte in a
end

; Put back the bank `value`, which map() gave. A, X, Y and the flags are kept.
pub asm func unmap(value: byte in y)
end
